    },
    "faq_gfYcTY": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "question_WVn3Wy": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Are glass chair mats durable enough for daily office use?",
            "text": "<p>Absolutely. Our glass chair mats at Clearly Innovative are built from quarter-inch-thick tempered glass, a material that goes through a heat-treatment process, making it four to five times stronger than standard glass. That translates to a surface that can support up to 1,000 pounds and hold up to the constant rolling, shifting, and daily pressure that comes with full-time desk work. What sets tempered glass apart is its ability to maintain its integrity over time. Plastic mats develop ruts, crack along stress points, and often start to bow or discolor within months of regular use. Our glass mats do none of that. The surface stays flat, clear, and smooth, no matter how many hours you put in. For someone working from home or spending long days at a corporate workstation, that kind of reliability matters. You are not buying something you will replace in a year or two. You are making a one-time investment in a mat that performs consistently day after day, year after year, without any degradation in quality or appearance. That is what daily durability actually looks like.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_LGU8xY": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can a glass chair mat be used on carpet or hard flooring?",
            "text": "<p>Yes, and that versatility is one of the things we hear customers appreciate most. At Clearly Innovative, our glass chair mats are designed to perform well on all standard floor types, including hardwood, carpet, laminate, tile, vinyl, and concrete. You do not need a different mat for different rooms or setups. For carpet installations, each mat ships with Velcro attachments that anchor it securely against the pile and prevent unwanted movement. For hard-surface floors like hardwood or tile, we include plastic holding discs that keep the mat stable through friction without causing any marking or damage to the surface below. The mat itself rests on a smooth underside that is safe for finished floors when installed correctly. One thing worth noting: always place the mat carefully rather than dragging it into position, and keep the underside clear of any debris before setting it down. Both of those habits go a long way toward protecting your floors. Whether your workspace has plush carpet or polished hardwood, your Clearly Innovative glass chair mat will work exactly the way it should.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_xnpkLw": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Will a glass chair mat slide or shift during use?",
            "text": "<p>No. This is a concern many people have before they experience a glass mat firsthand, and it is easy to understand why. Glass does not sound like something that would stay put. In practice, however, our mats are remarkably stable. A Clearly Innovative glass chair mat is a substantial piece of equipment. Depending on the size you choose, your mat can weigh close to 47 pounds or more, and that weight alone keeps it planted in most situations. Beyond that, every mat comes with both Velcro tabs for carpeted floors and plastic holding discs for hard surfaces. The Velcro grips into carpet fibers to prevent any lateral movement, while the holding discs create enough friction on smooth floors to keep the mat exactly where you put it. Customers who have switched from lightweight plastic mats often comment on how different the experience feels. There is no shifting underfoot, no mat creeping out of position throughout the day, and no need to constantly reposition it. Once it is set up correctly, it stays put. That kind of day-to-day reliability adds up over time and makes a genuine difference in your workspace comfort.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_MYPFwY": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Do glass chair mats protect floors from chair damage?",
            "text": "<p>Yes, and they do it more effectively than most alternatives. Every time an office chair rolls across an unprotected floor, the casters create friction, pressure, and wear on the surface beneath. Over hardwood, that means scratches and scuffs. Over carpet, it means flattened fibers, worn pathways, and eventual thinning of the pile. A glass chair mat from Clearly Innovative sits between your chair and your floor, absorbing all of that daily movement without transferring damage downward. The smooth, rigid surface of tempered glass distributes the weight of your chair and body evenly, rather than concentrating pressure on specific contact points as hard casters can. That even distribution is much gentler on the flooring over time. Our mats also feature a patented beveled edge, which lies flat against the floor rather than sitting at a sharp angle. That design detail prevents the mat's edges from digging into or scraping the floor during normal use, which is a common problem with cheaper alternatives that have abrupt, squared-off edges. Your floors stay looking good longer, and you never have to worry about the mat itself causing damage. That is protection that actually works in practice, not just in theory.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_Jcb4DC": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Why choose a glass chair mat instead of plastic?",
            "text": "<p>The best answer is longevity and performance. Plastic chair mats are inexpensive upfront, but they tend to fail quickly under regular use. They crack along the edges, develop deep wheel grooves, curl at the corners, and turn cloudy or yellowed over time. Most people who use a plastic mat in a home office or professional setting end up replacing it within a year or two, sometimes sooner. That replacement cost adds up. A Clearly Innovative glass chair mat does not do any of those things. Made from quarter-inch tempered glass that is four to five times stronger than regular glass and rated to hold up to 1,000 pounds, the surface resists gouging, maintains its clarity, and holds its shape indefinitely. Your chair rolls more smoothly on glass than it ever will on a worn plastic mat, which also carries real ergonomic benefits. Physical therapists have recognized that smooth chair movement reduces the strain placed on your back, knees, and hips throughout the workday. Beyond the practical side, glass simply looks better. It is clean, modern, and works with any office decor without drawing attention to itself. When you factor in the lifetime warranty we back every mat with, the value picture becomes very clear. You pay more once and never deal with the problem again. That is a trade most people are glad they made.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_Jf8D7P": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Are glass chair mats resistant to scratches?",
            "text": "<p>Our glass chair mats hold up very well against the kind of everyday surface contact that comes with normal office use. Tempered glass is a dense, hard material, and chair casters rolling across it day after day will not leave marks or wear down the surface the way they would on plastic or vinyl. Unlike plastic mats, you will not see the cloudy patches, deep wheel grooves, or that worn-out appearance that tends to show up after just a few months of regular use. That said, no material is completely impervious under all conditions. The most common culprit is grit or fine debris, such as sand or small particles tracked in from outside, that gets caught between the casters and the mat surface. If abrasive material is ground repeatedly into the glass, it can eventually leave fine marks. The good news is that this is easy to prevent with a quick wipe-down using a standard glass cleaner every so often, which removes any accumulated debris and keeps the surface in good shape. With basic care, your Clearly Innovative glass mat will maintain its scratch resistance and stay looking as good as the day it arrived. Browse our full range to find the right size and shape for your space.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_ssAmz1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Will a glass chair mat crack, warp, or turn yellow over time?",
            "text": "<p>No. Unlike plastic or vinyl chair mats that crack, curl, and yellow within months, a ¼\" tempered glass chair mat is engineered to stay perfectly flat and crystal clear. Backed by a Limited Lifetime guarantee, no warping, no discoloration.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_ssAmz2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Will my office chair roll smoothly on a glass mat?",
            "text": "<p>Yes. Our glass chair mats feature patented 1\" beveled edges with rounded 3\" radius corners so your chair glides on and off smoothly in every direction, no wheel catching, no cupping, no mat shifting. Chair wheels are protected, and the mat stays in place.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
